  "id": "visual-illusion",
  "term": "visual illusion",
  "definition": "A visual illusion is a false interpretation of what is seen, so that motion, direction, speed, or the source of movement is perceived incorrectly. In this historical usage, the error often depends on relative visual conditions, such as where the eyes are fixed or how surrounding objects are seen.",
